// `deep` as a consult with no card, 2026-11-21, on Adam's request: "can you make it that it doesn't
// need to ask my permission, just make it work". jorah-guard asked Adam before every hand-off to
// `deep` from a chat that had read outside text, because `deep` had a sandboxed shell with
// internet, so a brief could carry data out past the URL rule. In Adam's one long chat that was
// every hand-off after the first. `deep` doesn't need a shell: its only exec calls (guard log,
// 13 to 21 Nov) were its own hourly heartbeats. So it loses the shell, file writes and the
// sessions tools; jorah-guard enforces the same (matrix.consultAgents) and lets main ask it freely.
// What's left: read and ls in its own sandbox workspace, web_search, web_fetch, x_search,
// price_compare, view_image, session_status.
// Managed claude-cli turns expose none of Claude's own tools (docs/gateway/cli-backends.md,
// "Managed turns expose no Claude-native tools by default"), so this removes the shell for real.
// Arrays are replaced, so the deny list repeats the four entries from front.patch.json5.
//
// Code Mode off, 2026-11-22. Adam's first Telegram consult worked, but `deep` answered without
// the web: the guard blocked its `exec` (08:50:41). A spawned `deep` runs on the embedded runtime
// (a sandboxed child can't use claude-cli), and there OpenClaw's "auto" Code Mode engages for
// Opus: the model sees only `exec`/`wait` and calls web_search from JavaScript
// (docs/tools/code-mode.md). That `exec` is not a shell, but its default Node executor "is not a
// security boundary" and runs on the Gateway host, outside Podman. So Code Mode stays off for
// `deep`: it gets Tool Search (`tool_call`), which jorah-guard unwraps and checks per inner tool.
// Undo for both: tools.deny as above and `config unset agents.entries.deep.tools.codeMode`.
{
  agents: {
    entries: {
      deep: {
        tools: {
          codeMode: false,
          deny: [
            "image_generate", "video_generate", "music_generate", "message",
            "exec", "process", "write", "edit", "apply_patch",
            "sessions_list", "sessions_history", "sessions_search", "sessions_send", "sessions_spawn",
            "sessions_yield", "subagents",
          ],
        },
      },
    },
  },
}
